@startuml

salt
{
  <b>ORE STUDIO - REPORTING: SCHEDULE</b>
  --
  <b>DEFINITION: Group Consolidated Exposure - ACMCOR</b>
  --
  {#
    Type | Party | Latest run
    risk | ACMCOR | completed clean at 06:04:31
  }
  --
  <b>CURRENT SCHEDULE: ON DEMAND</b>
  --
  {#
    State | Schedule expression | Scheduler job
    on demand | - | none
  }
  {
    [ Set a schedule ]
  }
  --
  <b>SET A SCHEDULE</b>
  --
  {
    Expression [ 0 6 ~* ~* 1-5 ] | [ Schedule ]
  }
  Confirm: give Group Consolidated Exposure (ACMCOR) the schedule 0 6 ~* ~* 1-5?
  {
    [ Cancel ] | [ Schedule ]
  }
  --
  <b>AFTER THE WRITE: SCHEDULED</b>
  --
  {#
    State | Schedule expression | Scheduler job
    scheduled | 0 6 ~* ~* 1-5 | a job id from scheduler_job_id
  }
  {
    [ Change the expression ] | [ Unschedule ]
  }
  The panel states that the definition is scheduled because scheduler_job_id is
  set. The next firing creates a run, and the run appears on the front door.
  --
  <b>CHANGE THE EXPRESSION</b>
  --
  {
    Expression [ 0 7 ~* ~* 1-5 ] | [ Schedule ]
  }
  The same operation is sent with the new expression. The service reconciles the
  definition's schedule; the screen reads the definition back and states the
  result.
  --
  <b>UNSCHEDULE</b>
  --
  {
    Take the schedule away from Group Consolidated Exposure (ACMCOR)?
  }
  {
    [ Cancel ] | [ Unschedule ]
  }
  --
  <b>AFTER THE WRITE: ON DEMAND AGAIN</b>
  --
  {#
    State | Schedule expression | Scheduler job | Past runs
    on demand | 0 7 ~* ~* 1-5 | none | kept
  }
  The definition stays and can still be run now. The runs already produced keep
  their outputs and their errors. Unscheduling does not stop a run in flight, and
  there is no operation here that cancels one.
  --
  <b>WHAT THIS PANEL CANNOT SHOW</b>
  --
  Last fired: not readable. Next due: not readable. The firing is a
  report_trigger_event and no read of it exists; the scheduler job's state is
  not read either. The schedule expression carries no time zone, so the panel
  cannot say whose clock reads it. The screen states these absences rather than
  inventing a next-run time.
}

@enduml
